[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{4}[t])=5.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a8bf202-99c5-5bfd-8df3-5bd27cd65640" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of a Polynomial Vector Space Given Its Standard Monomial Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a2070b-ee01-5111-a61c-4347e5d15c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483595} {:answer/id #uuid "14be6a81-848a-5ae7-b43b-71982638b4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483602} {:answer/id #uuid "71cae8a4-5a70-59fa-850b-21fa607637c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483791} {:answer/id #uuid "7427b7f3-6b05-5734-9feb-603f47022317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483800} {:answer/id #uuid "d039d520-3a75-55a1-9af7-a275fca2bb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71cae8a4-5a70-59fa-850b-21fa607637c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483791} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ae82675-ac3d-59f8-b4e1-4558ec943bfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d3c2164-c9a8-58f5-b6ac-e24eb41f738f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95212" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{10}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{10}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a8bf202-99c5-5bfd-8df3-5bd27cd65640" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of a Polynomial Vector Space Given Its Standard Monomial Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6d5be9-5fde-5bb9-9bee-f918be995699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483613} {:answer/id #uuid "328814cb-04ed-5e28-9136-e52ad092621f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483657} {:answer/id #uuid "544af5b2-e568-5879-9dfc-1771789af078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483718} {:answer/id #uuid "7853074c-edb6-52a0-b062-c5e4c14a5deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483812} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cce873-2161-5984-acce-f8d8414e627a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "121" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7853074c-edb6-52a0-b062-c5e4c14a5deb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483812} :answer-field/id #uuid "38c2ea0e-22d7-5c6c-aa9f-6f8f2f79b01c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "097f3ed9-cfa8-5b5e-b19c-f247430007b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-95213" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${R}_{11}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $11?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{11}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{11}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{11}[t])=11+1=12.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b61a755f-23e8-5039-b2f5-b5984fdb420c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of a Matrix Vector Space Given Its Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "004ea4df-4a63-51f5-8a95-4918c77bb235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483569} {:answer/id #uuid "06e3275e-bbed-543d-8acb-c7b93e0675b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483583} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1c5938-4bed-5f27-9ba7-b5019d35613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483776} {:answer/id #uuid "b15605a4-a0e0-5b34-ad32-57316442f845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,225" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483919} {:answer/id #uuid "f87f54a3-e5d0-5865-8bdd-749397d547f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c1c5938-4bed-5f27-9ba7-b5019d35613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483776} :answer-field/id #uuid "58be5a47-1791-51fb-bc85-5571daaceba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e90af7eb-4ed1-5ce3-8ebf-5e64d3a26828" :question/math-academy-id "q-95214" :question/problem "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{5\\times 7}(R),$ the vector space of all $5\\times 7$ matrices over $R?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R)$ contains a total of $n\\cdot m$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{3\\times 2}(R)$ contains $3\\cdot 2=6$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{5\\times 7}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{5\\times 7}(R))=5\\cdot 7=35.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152222 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b61a755f-23e8-5039-b2f5-b5984fdb420c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of a Matrix Vector Space Given Its Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{: